; Stage 15 W9 item 7: a `CStr` carries NO non-null contract, so it may not flow
; into a typed non-null slot.
;
; `pkind-flow-check` fired only for a `TY-PTR` source. `CStr` is `TY-CSTR`, so it
; fell out of the check entirely and this line compiled clean, stored a null in a
; slot whose type says it can never be null, and segfaulted on first use — in the
; GLOBAL position here and in the identical local (w9-cstr-into-ref-let.nuc).
;
; The exemption this replaces was recorded as "a C string is a non-null
; constant". That is true of a string LITERAL and false of the type: `getenv`
; returns a `CStr` and returns null.
;
; The other direction is still legal and is pinned by w5c-cstr-null-exempt.nuc:
; a null INTO a `CStr` slot is ordinary C.
(defstruct W9C7 n:i32)

(defvar g-bad:ptr:W9C7 (as CStr null))

(defn main ():i32
  (return (g-bad n)))
